```
- Line 1 has a mistake in it :: Line 1 is correct: a lowercase `print`, a pair of brackets, and text in quotes.
- print() only shows its output when the whole program has finished :: print shows its output straight away. In a program with a NameError or a TypeError, the lines before the error do appear.
* Python reads the whole file before running it, and line 3 has a SyntaxError :: Right. Line 3 is missing its closing bracket. Python checks every line before it runs any of them, so the program never starts.
- Python stops at the first error, and an error stops every line, even the ones before it :: Errors that happen while the program runs leave the earlier output on the screen. Only an error found while reading the file stops everything.
