labels: 1st run | 2nd run | 3rd run
answer: SyntaxError | NameError | TypeError
wrong[NameError | TypeError | SyntaxError]: Python reads the whole file before running it, so the missing bracket on line 4 is reported first, before the program even starts. Only then do the errors on lines 1 and 3 appear, from top to bottom.
wrong[NameError | SyntaxError | TypeError]: The SyntaxError on line 4 stops the program before any line runs, so it's reported on the very first run, before the NameError on line 1.
