hint: The four bugs are: a missing bracket, spaces at the start of a line, a string and a number joined with `+`, and a capital letter.
hint: For the Serves line, use commas: `print("Serves", 4, "people")`. print adds the spaces for you.
right: Four bugs, four error types. Python found the SyntaxError and the IndentationError while reading the file, so the first two runs printed nothing. The TypeError and the NameError showed up only while running, after the lines above them had printed. Each fix revealed the next error, because Python always stops at the first one.
wrong: Work through the errors one at a time, in the order Python reports them: read the last line of the report, go to the line number it gives, fix that one problem, and submit again. The error type tells you what to look for: SyntaxError means a missing bracket or quote, IndentationError means spaces at the start of a line, TypeError means a string and a number joined with `+`, and NameError means a misspelled or wrongly capitalized name.

